# Transcript conventions

When working with YouTube transcripts:

1. Prefer YouTubeTranscript.dev API for extraction (captions first, AI fallback).
2. Store transcripts as `.txt` for plain text, `.srt`/`.vtt` for timed captions, `.json` for structured data.
3. Include video ID and language in filenames when saving (e.g. `dQw4w9WgXcQ-en.txt`).
4. Preserve timestamps when format matters; strip when only content is needed.
